  "body": "Some years ago, W3C has loosened the Content model for the `legend` element, [allowing headings](https://github.com/w3c/html/commit/943d518284f1a027c7ccfa889ec510ccb6f2f60c) in addition to phrasing content in it. There seems to be some evidence that [it helps accessibility](https://www.accessibility-developer-guide.com/examples/forms/grouping-with-headings/), and this usage is quite often [promoted](https://twitter.com/webaxe/status/1181631279608918016) as the useful and W3C-approved practice. Isn't this change worth porting into the Living Standard?",
